# Preserve the final Unreal session

- After the final screenshot, render or visual-proof capture, leave Unreal
  Editor and the YACS project open for the owner's manual inspection.
- Do not stop the editor process, close the project or run final cleanup that
  destroys the inspection state.
- When practical, leave the captured map, camera and relevant viewport state
  visible at handoff.
- Helper processes may be stopped when they are not needed to keep the editor
  and project available.
- If an automation normally shuts Unreal down, disable that final cleanup or
  reopen the target project and map before handoff.
- Close or restart Unreal only when the owner explicitly requests it or when a
  restart is required to complete the requested work. Report an unavoidable
  restart and restore the inspection state afterward when possible.
- The final status must say whether Unreal was left open and identify the map
  or view prepared for inspection.
